{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>If you afflict him.</b> This is an abbreviated verse — it cut short and did not specify his punishment, like ״לָכֵן כָּל הֹרֵג קַיִן״ (Genesis 4) — it cut short and did not specify his punishment. So too here, ״אִם עַנֵּה תְעַנֵּה אֹתוֹ״ is an expression of cutting short: that is, will you ultimately take what is yours? — for ״כִּי אִם צָעֹק יִצְעַק אֵלַי״ and so forth."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:57.369182172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}